---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const aboutPhoto = 'data:image/webp;base64,';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Tessa Rouse, an MPA candidate, political science graduate, U.S. Army veteran, and emerging public administration and policy professional."
>
  <section class="page-section about-hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Public service shaped the path. Policy gave it direction.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I'm Tessa Rouse, a U.S. Army veteran, political science graduate, and Master of
          Public Administration candidate at Arizona State University.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work sits at the intersection of policy analysis, public administration,
          organizational systems, data quality, and service delivery. I'm especially interested
          in what happens after a policy is adopted: how institutions interpret it, implement it,
          measure it, and translate it into an experience people can actually navigate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="about-photo">
        <img src={aboutPhoto} alt="Tessa Rouse smiling in academic regalia" width="256" height="256" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">The throughline</p>
        <h2>Systems, responsibility, and implementation.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="story-copy">
        <p>
          I began my professional life in the U.S. Army as a Network Switch Systems Operator.
          The work centered on communications readiness, equipment accountability, operational
          support, and emergency preparedness—including overseas service supporting Patriot
          missile operations.
        </p>
        <p>
          After leaving the Army, I worked in safety, security, emergency response, and
          operational-support environments. Those roles required documentation, adherence to
          policy and procedure, incident coordination, stakeholder communication, and the ability
          to make sound decisions when conditions changed quickly.
        </p>
        <p>
          My later work in emergency response coordination added GIS-based mapping, compliance
          databases, data quality assurance, auditing, reporting, and process improvement. That
          experience helped clarify the kind of work I wanted to pursue long term: understanding
          public systems, finding where they break down, and helping improve how decisions are
          implemented.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section academic-section">
    <div class="container academic-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Academic direction</p>
        <h2>From political science to public administration.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="academic-copy">
        <p>
          I earned a B.A. in Political Science, with a concentration in American Government,
          from American Military University in February 2026, graduating Cum Laude.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am now completing a Master of Public Administration at Arizona State University,
          where my graduate work has focused on policy analysis, governance, ethics,
          organizational management, research methods, statistics, implementation, and public
          service.
        </p>
        <p>
          The shift from political science to public administration was deliberate. Political
          science gave me a framework for understanding institutions and power; public
          administration asks the question I find even more compelling: <em>how do we make those
          institutions work well in practice?</em>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section focus-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Current focus</p>
          <h2>The work I want to keep doing.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          I'm building toward policy, program, management, and administrative analysis roles
          where research and evidence can improve public-sector decisions and implementation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="focus-grid">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Policy & program analysis</h3>
          <p>Researching public problems, evaluating alternatives, and translating evidence into useful analysis.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Administrative systems</h3>
          <p>Examining workflows, implementation capacity, organizational responsibility, and administrative burden.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Data & operations</h3>
          <p>Using data quality, GIS support, documentation, and process analysis to strengthen operational decision-making.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section personal-section">
    <div class="container personal-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Outside the work</p>
        <h2>Still a person, fortunately.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="personal-copy">
        <p class="lede">
          A professional site should say something about the person behind the résumé, too.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside of school and policy work, I'm usually somewhere near a theme park, a
          camera, or a game console. Photography gives me an excuse to pay attention to small
          details; the rest mostly gives my brain somewhere else to go.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    padding-top: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
  }

  .hero-grid,
  .story-grid,
  .academic-grid,
  .personal-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 8rem);
  }

  .hero-grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(15rem, 0.65fr);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .story-grid,
  .academic-grid,
  .personal-grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
  }

  .academic-grid,
  .personal-grid {
    align-items: end;
  }

  .hero-copy > :first-child,
  .academic-copy > :first-child,
  .personal-copy > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .about-photo {
    width: min(100%, 20rem);
    margin: 0;
    justify-self: end;
    position: relative;
  }

  .about-photo::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0.7rem -0.7rem -0.7rem 0.7rem;
    z-index: -1;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: 1.35rem;
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }

  .about-photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: 1.2rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .hero-copy p:not(.lede),
  .story-copy p,
  .academic-copy p,
  .personal-copy p:not(.lede) {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .section-title {
    position: sticky;
    top: 7rem;
    align-self: start;
  }

  .section-title h2,
  .academic-grid h2,
  .personal-grid h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
  }

  .story-copy {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
  }

  .story-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .academic-section,
  .personal-section {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-bg-deep) 58%, transparent);
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    align-items: end;
    gap: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .section-heading h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    max-width: 11ch;
  }

  .section-heading > p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .focus-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
  }

  .focus-grid article {
    padding: 1.7rem 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .focus-grid article + article {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .focus-grid span {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .focus-grid h3 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
  }

  .focus-grid p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .hero-grid,
    .story-grid,
    .academic-grid,
    .personal-grid,
    .section-heading {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .about-photo {
      width: min(78vw, 19rem);
      justify-self: start;
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .section-title {
      position: static;
    }

    .focus-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .focus-grid article,
    .focus-grid article + article {
      padding: 1.5rem 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .focus-grid span {
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
